### OhMyFreezer — Platform Admin API runbook
###
### Manual for the platform superadmin (single operator). NOT a Usuario, NOT
### tenant-scoped — see sdd/negocio-onboarding-admin design D1. Compatible
### with the IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code "REST Client" extension:
### open this file and click "Send Request" above each block, or run each
### block with `curl` as documented below it.
###
### ── One-time setup: ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH ────────────────────────────────────
###
### 1. Pick a strong random secret (this IS your plaintext admin credential,
###    never commit it anywhere):
###
###      openssl rand -base64 32
###
### 2. Hash it with the SAME BCryptPasswordEncoder the app already uses (do
###    NOT hash it with an external tool — the format must match exactly).
###    Quickest way, from the backend/ directory with a running JVM:
###
###      jshell --class-path target/classes:$(./mvnw -q dependency:build-classpath -Dmdep.outputFile=/dev/stdout)
###      > new org.springframework.security.crypto.bcrypt.BCryptPasswordEncoder().encode("YOUR_PLAINTEXT_SECRET")
###
###    (Or write a 3-line throwaway @Test that prints the hash — that's how
###    test/resources/application.properties' own token-hash was generated,
###    see NegocioAdminServiceTest / AdminContainmentIntegrationTest headers.)
###
### 3. Set the resulting bcrypt hash (starts with $2a$/$2b$/$2y$) as an
###    environment variable on the server, NEVER in application.properties:
###
###      ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH=$2a$10$...................................
###
###    Leaving it unset (or blank) hard-disables ALL of /api/admin/** with a
###    fail-closed 403 on every request — see AdminApiKeyFilter Javadoc / design D2.
###    A non-blank value that is NOT a valid bcrypt hash makes the app refuse
###    to start (fail loud, not a silently-broken secret).
###
### 4. Every request below carries the PLAINTEXT secret from step 1 (never
###    the hash) in the X-Admin-Token header — set it once here:

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = YOUR_PLAINTEXT_SECRET_HERE

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1. Create a Negocio + its first signup code (atomic)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/negocios
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Cocina Central",
  "emailContacto": "contacto@cocinacentral.com"
}

# curl equivalent:
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/negocios \
#   -H "X-Admin-Token: $ADMIN_TOKEN" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"nombre":"Cocina Central","emailContacto":"contacto@cocinacentral.com"}'
#
# Response 201: { "negocio": {...}, "signupCode": { "codigo": "XXXXXXXXXX", ... } }
# Relay signupCode.codigo to the jefe MANUALLY (WhatsApp/email) — the API
# never sends anything automatically (confirmed assumption #3).

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2. Mint an additional signup code for an existing Negocio
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### No cap on simultaneously valid codes; allowed even after the first jefe
### of that Negocio has already registered (e.g. re-onboarding a lost account).

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/negocios/1/signup-codes
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

# curl equivalent:
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/negocios/1/signup-codes \
#   -H "X-Admin-Token: $ADMIN_TOKEN"
#
# Response 201: { "id": ..., "codigo": "...", "negocioId": 1, "usado": false, "activo": true, ... }
# Response 404 if the Negocio id doesn't exist.

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3. List all Negocios (most recent first)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/negocios
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

# curl equivalent:
# curl http://localhost:8080/api/admin/negocios \
#   -H "X-Admin-Token: $ADMIN_TOKEN"

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4. List all signup codes of a Negocio (used, unused and revoked)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/negocios/1/signup-codes
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

# curl equivalent:
# curl http://localhost:8080/api/admin/negocios/1/signup-codes \
#   -H "X-Admin-Token: $ADMIN_TOKEN"
#
# Response 404 if the Negocio id doesn't exist.

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5. Revoke a signup code
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Revoking does NOT disable any account already created with that code —
### it only prevents FUTURE registrations from consuming it. Semantics:
###   - active + unused   -> 200, now activo=false
###   - already revoked   -> 200, idempotent no-op
###   - already used      -> 409 Conflict (revoking a used code is a no-op
###                          on the account it already created; disable the
###                          Usuario separately if that's the real intent)
###   - unknown id         -> 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/signup-codes/1/revoke
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

# curl equivalent:
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/admin/signup-codes/1/revoke \
#   -H "X-Admin-Token: $ADMIN_TOKEN"

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Rejection reference (see AdminContainmentIntegrationTest /
### NegocioAdminEndpointsAuthMatrixIntegrationTest for the exhaustive suite)
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### - No X-Admin-Token header                          -> 403
### - Wrong X-Admin-Token value                          -> 403
### - ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH unset/blank on the server         -> 403 for every request
### - A valid tenant JWT (Authorization: Bearer ...)      -> 403 on /api/admin/**
### - A valid X-Admin-Token on any NON-admin route
###   (e.g. GET /api/ingredientes)                        -> 403, never tenant data
